./ ALIAS NAME=AU                                                                
)F FUNCTION -                                                                   
  The ADDUSER command defines a new RAKF user.  It writes one line per          
  group into the USERS member of SYS1.SECURE.CNTL and a record into             
  SYS1.SECURE.SHADOW holding an 8 byte salt and sha-256(salt||password).        
  no clear text password is ever stored.  The command fails if the user         
  already exists - use ALTUSER to change one.                                   
                                                                                
  ADDUSER updates the control data sets on disk only.  Reload the in            
  core tables afterwards with 'S RAKFUSER' from the console, or by              
  running the RAKFUSER procedure in batch, or the new user cannot log           
  on yet.                                                                       
                                                                                
  You must be connected to the RAKFADM group.  ADDUSER is an ordinary           
  problem state program - it is the protection on the control data sets         
  that enforces this, not APF authorization.                                    
)X SYNTAX -                                                                     
  ADDUSER userid PASSWORD(pw) DFLTGRP(group)                                    
          | GROUP(g2 g3 ...) | OPERATIONS   | SPECIAL                           
                             | NOOPERATIONS | NOSPECIAL                         
                                                                                
  REQUIRED - userid, PASSWORD, DFLTGRP                                          
  DEFAULT  - NOOPERATIONS, NOSPECIAL                                            
                                                                                
  All input is folded to upper case.                                            
                                                                                
  Examples from a TSO session:                                                  
                                                                                
    ADDUSER SMITH PASSWORD(START123) DFLTGRP(USER)                              
                                                                                
    ADDUSER JONES PASSWORD(HUNTER2) DFLTGRP(ADMIN) +                            
            GROUP(RAKFADM) OPERATIONS                                           
                                                                                
  The operands can be shortened to the shortest unique abbreviation.            
  So, ADDUSER JONES P(HUNTER2) D(ADMIN) G(RAKFADM) O                            
  is also valid.                                                                
                                                                                
                                                                                
  In batch, invoke it from the TMP so the load module is found, and             
  supply all of these DD statements:                                            
                                                                                
    //ADDUSER  EXEC PGM=IKJEFT01,REGION=4096K                                   
    //SYSPRINT DD  SYSOUT=*                                                     
    //SYSTERM  DD  SYSOUT=*                                                     
    //SYSIN    DD  DUMMY                                                        
    //SYSTSPRT DD  SYSOUT=*                                                     
    //SYSTSIN  DD  *                                                            
     ADDUSER 'SMITH PASSWORD(START123) DFLTGRP(USER)'                           
    /*                                                                          
                                                                                
  Keep the command within column 72 and continue with a plus sign.              
                                                                                
  Every one of those dd statements matters:                                     
                                                                                
  SYSPRINT, SYSTERM and SYSIN are opened before the command itself              
  starts.  If any cannot be opened the program ends immediately, so             
  the step fails with rc=12 and an empty SYSTSPRT - no message at all           
  explaining why.                                                               
                                                                                
  USERS and SHADOW are dynamically allocated. SYS1.SECURE.* is                  
  protected with UACC(NONE), so the user needs the RAKFADM group.               
  The command reports "RAKFUSER access denied" or                               
  "RAKFSHAD access denied" if trying to run with a group other                  
  than RAKFADM.                                                                 
                                                                                
  RETURN CODES:                                                                 
                                                                                
     0 - The user was added.                                                    
     8 - An error occurs. A suitable message will be given to                   
         the user.                                                              
)O OPERANDS -                                                                   
))USERID - the user to create.  1 to 8 characters.  Required, and must          
  be the first operand.  If a user of this name already exists the              
  command ends with return code 8 and the user will be notified.                
))PASSWORD - PASSWORD(pw) supplies the initial password.  Required.             
  1 to 8 characters.  It is salted and hashed by the same routine the           
  logon path uses, so the stored digest and a later logon attempt are           
  compared byte for byte.                                                       
  An alias of PASSWORD is PWD.                                                  
))DFLTGRP - DFLTGRP(group) names the default group.  Required.  1 to 8          
  characters.  The users line for this group carries the '*' default            
  flag.  A line is written for this group whether or not it is also             
  named on group.                                                               
  An alias of DFLTGRP is DGRP.                                                  
))GROUP - GROUP(g2 g3 ...) connects the user to further groups, one             
  users line each.  Optional.  Separate the names with blanks inside            
  the parentheses.  Each name may be up to 8 characters names.                  
  At most 5 groups are kept.                                                    
  An alias of GROUP is GRP.                                                     
))OPERATIONS - marks every line of the user with the operations                 
  attribute (Y).  Optional.  The default is NOOPERATONS with                    
  the attribute (N).                                                            
))SPECIAL - marks every line of the user with the SPECIAL attribute             
  (y).  Optional.  The default is NOSPECIAL with attribute(N).                  
                                                                                
